---

<section class="cta" id="install">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="tile">
      <img src="/brand/moodle-mcp-icon.svg" alt="moodle-mcp icon" />
    </div>
    <h2><span class="grad-mcp">Your Moodle, one prompt away</span></h2>
    <p class="sub">Single binary. Twenty tools. Zero browser tabs.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a
        class="btn btn-primary"
        href="https://github.com/G36maid/moodle-mcp/releases/latest"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path
            d="M8 1v9m0 0L4.5 6.5M8 10l3.5-3.5M2 13.5h12"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
        </svg>
        Download now <span class="kbd">D</span>
      </a>
      <a
        class="btn btn-ghost"
        href="https://github.com/G36maid/moodle-mcp"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
          <path
            d="M5.5 10.5 10.5 5.5m-4 0h4v4"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.6"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"></path>
        </svg>
        Clone source <span class="kbd">C</span>
      </a>
    </div>
    <p class="hint">or <code>cargo install moodle-mcp</code> — needs Rust 1.88+</p>
    <details class="oneprompt">
      <summary>One-prompt install — paste into your agent chat</summary>
      <pre><code>Set up moodle-mcp for me. First read https://moodle.ntnu.cc/docs/installation.html
and https://moodle.ntnu.cc/docs/configuration.html. Then install the binary
for my platform (prefer the prebuilt archive from the latest GitHub release;
cargo install moodle-mcp as the fallback), run moodle-mcp auth in the
terminal so I can type my school credentials when it prompts, and register
the server in your own MCP config — name "moodle", stdio command moodle-mcp,
env MOODLE_URL and MOODLE_TOKEN from auth's output. Do not store or repeat
my credentials anywhere.</code></pre>
      <p class="hint">Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, OpenCode, pi — the agent installs the
      binary, opens <code>moodle-mcp auth</code> in its terminal (you type the
      credentials there, not in the chat), and writes its own client
      config.</p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .cta {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    text-align: center;
    background:
      radial-gradient(circle at 50% 0%, rgba(19, 72, 220, 0.05), transparent 55%);
  }

  .inner {
    padding: 72px var(--gutter) 84px;
  }

  .tile {
    width: 112px;
    margin: 0 auto 30px;
    border-radius: 24px;
    box-shadow:
      0 0 0 1px var(--line),
      0 18px 40px rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.28);
  }

  .tile img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 24px;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 34px;
    
  }

  .sub {
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    font-size: 15px;
  }

  .actions {
    margin-top: 32px;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 14px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  .oneprompt {
    margin-top: 18px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .oneprompt summary {
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--ink-2, #5b6472);
    padding: 8px 0;
  }
  .oneprompt pre {
    background: var(--panel, #f6f7f9);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 14px 16px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    line-height: 1.55;
    overflow-x: auto;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  .oneprompt .hint {
    margin-top: 8px;
  }
  .hint {
    margin: 24px 0 0;
    font-size: 13px;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .hint code {
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 4px;
    padding: 1px 7px;
    color: var(--ink-strong);
  }
</style>
